<%# The contact form. It is here, as a plain ERB partial, and not in the body of the `contact` page
    in Contentful. markdown_to_html renders that body through the SmartyPants of Redcarpet (refer to
    lib/helpers/markdown_helpers.rb), which makes each straight quotation mark in a raw HTML
    *attribute* curly. That breaks the field names of the form and its Stimulus attributes. The
    intro text above the form stays in Contentful, where a person can edit it.
    partials/article/_body.html.erb adds this partial to the contact page.

    Keep the field names — name, email, message, and the honeypot `comment` — the same as in the
    Api::ContactController of the api. Refer to the contact contract in the root CLAUDE.md. This form
    also works with no JavaScript: the method and the action do a native POST, then a 303 to
    /contact/success. With JavaScript, the `contact` Stimulus controller takes the submit, does a
    fetch, and shows a toast. %>
<form method="POST" action="/api/contact" class="form"
      data-controller="contact" data-action="submit->contact#submit" data-turbo="false"
      data-contact-site-key-value="<%= turnstile_site_key %>">
  <wa-input label="Your name" type="text" name="name" autocomplete="name" with-clear required></wa-input>
  <wa-input label="Your email" type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" with-clear required></wa-input>
  <label class="hp">Comment <textarea name="comment" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></textarea></label>
  <wa-textarea label="What's on your mind?" name="message" rows="6" resize="auto" with-count required></wa-textarea>
  <%# Cloudflare Turnstile goes here. The `contact` controller renders it, and that render works
      with Turbo. It is empty or absent when there is no sitekey in the configuration, and the
      controller then omits it and the Turnstile check of the api permits the message. It protects
      the JavaScript path only, because the POST with no JavaScript cannot run the widget. %>
  <div class="contact__turnstile" data-contact-target="turnstile"></div>
  <wa-button type="submit" variant="brand" appearance="accent" data-contact-target="submit">
    Send Message
    <%= icon_svg("classic", "solid", "paper-plane")&.sub("<svg", '<svg slot="end"') %>
  </wa-button>
</form>
